sync rather than a raw copy; four P3s, one applied: an isSafeInteger guard in numeric-content-key's integer branch, mirroring exact's existing guard). Final verification after the fix: kondo 0/0, cljstyle clean, full JVM Java 17 1743 tests / 174922 assertions, CLJS 1660 tests / 44798 assertions, CLJD 1622 tests all passed. Committed 92103d8b, no trailers, hook changed nothing.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:7976:  \"design target, not implemented\"; dao.stream.ws.md accept/disclaim\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:10206:  aggregates the 166 generated Dart test files into 8 shards (Dart test phase 379 s -> about 140 s). The JFR profiling test was removed (it could not fail).\ntest/dao/postgraphics/packing_test.cljc:91:(defn- collect-into\ndocs/cross-language-macro.md:3:Status: **not implemented, and its `yin.vm.macro/expand-all` target is\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:181:aggregated lanes only run namespaces that still exist under `test/`, but a\ndocs/agents/known-gaps.md:32:| L-e (closure-origin and store-ownership verification) not implemented | docs 7.5 | linker | L-e | P1 |\ndocs/agents/#build-n-test.md#:181:aggregated lanes only run namespaces that still exist under `test/`, but a\ndocs/datomic.md:864:| `hasFulltext()` | `boolean` | True if fulltext index is maintained |\ntest/yang/python/antlr/int_heap_test.cljc:157:(defn- collection\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:873:(defn q [query space & {:keys [as-of inputs]}])     ; Datomic Datalog → set of tuples\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:925:(defn q [query space & {:keys [as-of inputs]}] (db/q query (fold-db space as-of)))\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:950:- **Tuples**: domain events `{:event/type :event/aggregate-id :event/data}`\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:951:- **Patterns**: \"events for aggregate X\", \"events since timestamp\", \"by event type\"\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:992:(deftest two-logs-aggregate-test\ntest/yang/python/antlr/import_test.cljc:1060:          [missing? import? diagnostics args uncached?] (vm/value done)]\